    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0797" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                        1893</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 61 of 19th ultimo
                    and the copy which you inclose of a letter from our consul at Sivas to our
                    consul-general at Constantinople, setting forth the unfriendly attitude and acts
                    of the vali of Sivas, in which province Marsovan is situate, toward Americans
                    there residing.</p>
                <p>The continuance and development of good will at Marsovan will largely depend, as
                    you point out, on the discretion and tact of the American officers of the
                    college, but their efforts to commend their enterprise as law-abiding and
                    beneficial to the community should not be neutralized by malevolent
                    misrepresentations and treatment such as is attributed, apparently of actual
                    knowledge, to the vali of Sivas.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
